// Title: VsCode Code Tunnel Execution File Indicator
// Sigma ID: 9661ec9d-4439-4a7a-abed-d9be4ca43b6d
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-10-25 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: command-and-control
// Tags: detection.threat-hunting
// Description: Detects the creation of a file with the name "code_tunnel.json" which indicate execution and
//   usage of VsCode tunneling utility. Attackers can abuse this functionality to establish a C2
//   channel
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate usage of VsCode tunneling functionality will also trigger this
// References:
//   - https://ipfyx.fr/post/visual-studio-code-tunnel/
//   - https://badoption.eu/blog/2023/01/31/code_c2.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules-threat-hunting/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_vscode_tunnel_indicators.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\code_tunnel.json"
